      "section": "### Mizzen: Tool-picker onboarding step with logo tile grid\n\nScreen types: account-setup, onboarding, integrations.\n\nAn onboarding question for an AI assistant workspace that asks which work tools the new member already uses. Picks are used to recommend connections later; nothing is connected yet. The page is deliberately sparse: one question, one explanatory line and nine tiles.\n\n#### Patterns\n- minimal onboarding top bar with repeated primary action\n- 3x3 selectable logo tile grid\n- multi-select tiles with focus glow\n- right-aligned next button\n- generous whitespace single-question screen\n\n#### Pages & layout\n1. **/join/tools** (this screen): 56px top bar with 'Joining Northwind Studio' (invented) and a compact Next. Centered column: heading 'Which tools does your team rely on?', description 'We'll suggest the right connections later. Pick as many as you like.', 3x3 grid of tiles (Team chat, Wiki, Knowledge base, Code host, CRM, Issue tracker, Shared inbox, Email, Mail and calendar) each with a generic colored glyph, then Next aligned right.\n2. Neighboring questions (role, team size) as stubs to show the flow.\n3. Mobile: 2-column grid, sticky bottom Next with safe-area padding.\n\n#### Components & interactions\n`OnboardingTopBar`, `QuestionHeader`, `ToolTile` (icon, name, check badge when pressed), `ToolGrid` (roving focus), `NextButton` (label switches Skip/Next). Hover lightens tile background; pressed adds tint, blue border, glow and check.\n\n#### Data & state\n`tools(id, name, icon_key, category)` seeded with nine generic tools; `onboarding_answers(user_id, question_key, tool_ids uuid[], answered_at)` with primary key (user_id, question_key). Local selection in React state, saved on Next with upsert. Preselect from existing answers.\n\n#### States to design\n- no selection (button reads Skip)\n- some selected\n- tool list loading (9 gray skeleton tiles)\n- tool list failed (fallback static list)\n- saving answers\n- save failed toast with retry\n- returning user sees previous picks pre-selected\n\n#### Guardrails\nUX:\n- One question per screen with a single primary action\n- Make selection state obvious with border, tint and a check, not color alone\n- Allow skipping without penalty\n- Explain in one line why the question is asked\n- Do not start any OAuth connection from this step\n- Persist picks so Back does not lose them\nAccessibility:\n- Grid is a group of toggle buttons with aria-pressed\n- Selected tiles show a check icon in addition to the border color\n- Roving tabindex with arrow-key navigation; Tab leaves the grid\n- Duplicate Next buttons share one accessible name and the top one is hidden on mobile\n- Focus ring 2px blue with 2px offset\n- Logos are decorative (alt empty) because the name is shown\nSecurity:\n- RLS: users can only read and write their own onboarding answers\n- Validate tool ids against the known list server-side\n- No third-party tokens are requested or stored on this step"
